    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented rejection of disposable email domains as an OfficeFloor function-injection step, following the project's endpoint conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `RejectDisposableEmailDomain.java` \u2014 a step that reads the published `OwnerFieldsDto`, extracts the domain after the final `@`, and throws `DisposableEmailDomainException` when the (lower-cased) domain is in the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Email is optional, so absent/blank is accepted. It runs after `NormalizeOwnerEmail`, which has already validated and lower-cased the address.\n- `DisposableEmailDomainException.java` \u2014 a checked exception (400).\n- `DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `400` with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`, mirroring the existing `InvalidEmailExceptionHandler`.\n- `...DisposableEmailDomainException.yml` \u2014 escalation wiring.\n\n**Wiring:** inserted a `rejectDisposableEmail` step immediately after `normalizeEmail` in both `owners.POST.yml` (create) and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (update), each governed by `transaction`, so the rule applies consistently to both create and update.",
